    "description": "The Order Service tracks fulfillment through Draft, Placed, Shipped, and Cancelled states. Today each order is a record with a status string, nullable payment reference, nullable shipping address, and nullable dispatch tracking number. Call sites construct these combinations directly, and validation happens only when an order is submitted or handed to the warehouse adapter. Consequently, a Draft can contain a payment reference, Shipped can lack tracking, and Cancelled can retain fulfillment data. The domain requires that each state expose only fields valid in that state, with no contradictory record constructible by application code. The Order API, Billing consumer, and Warehouse consumer must all consume the same state-specific representation. Decide how to encode the order lifecycle so construction rules are enforced centrally and downstream components can rely on the shape they receive without repeating validation.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose the representation that makes each order state carry only its valid fields and prevents callers from constructing contradictory lifecycle records.",
    "notes": "make-illegal-states-unrepresentable primary: per-state field validity must be impossible to violate by construction; sealed-case-class and algebraic-data-type are the representation near-misses; pattern-matching supports exhaustive downstream consumption."
  },
